 "final_message": "I made all twelve changes. The test suite passes (6 tests: the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted, and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** The README's `conversions_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries, and `daily_conversion_counts` has its own entry.\n- **Item 12:** The rest of the package did not follow the spec either, so I fixed it:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and returns keys in sorted order.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` now resets the run when a day has no flagged sessions.\n\nI tested only the two new cases and the existing tests, so most of the spec rules have no test of their own.\n\n- **Undefined cases:** The spec doesn't cover a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made that raise `ValueError` with the line number. A negative `days` in `conversions_in_window` returns `0`. A negative `n` in `top_converting_groups` returns an empty list.\n- **Not a git repository:** `/work` isn't one, so nothing is committed.",
